<% content_for :title, "Shinto | Bipolar Sober" %>

<style>
  /* ==========================================
     SHINTO — COMPLETE PAGE STYLES
     ========================================== */

  .st-page {
    --st-black: #080808;
    --st-pink: #ff1493;
    --st-yellow: #eaff00;
    --st-purple: #8a00ff;
    --st-white: #ffffff;

    width: 100%;
    margin: 0;
    background: var(--st-black);
    color: var(--st-white);
    font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
  }

  .st-page,
  .st-page *,
  .st-page *::before,
  .st-page *::after {
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }

  .st-page h1,
  .st-page h2,
  .st-page h3,
  .st-page p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* HERO */

  .st-page .st-hero {
    position: relative;
    isolation: isolate;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    min-height: 800px;
    min-height: max(800px, 100svh);
    padding: 130px 5vw 90px;
    background: var(--st-black);
  }

  .st-page .st-hero-picture {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: -2;
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
  }

  .st-page .st-hero-picture img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: right center;
  }

  .st-page .st-hero::after {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: -1;
    content: "";
    background:
      linear-gradient(
        90deg,
        rgba(8, 8, 8, 0.55),
        rgba(8, 8, 8, 0.1) 70%
      );
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .st-page .st-hero-content {
    width: 58%;
    max-width: 880px;
  }

  .st-page .st-eyebrow {
    margin-bottom: 32px;
    color: var(--st-yellow);
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 800;
    line-height: 1.6;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
  }

  .st-page .st-hero h1 {
    color: var(--st-white);
    font-size: clamp(64px, 7.4vw, 142px);
    font-weight: 900;
    line-height: 0.94;
    letter-spacing: -0.065em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .st-page .st-hero h1 span {
    display: block;
  }

  .st-page .st-intro {
    max-width: 540px;
    margin-top: 32px;
    color: var(--st-white);
    font-size: clamp(14px, 1.25vw, 19px);
    font-weight: 800;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  /* SECTIONS */

  .st-page .st-section {
    padding: 88px 5vw;
  }

  .st-page .st-inner {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.85fr) minmax(0, 1.15fr);
    align-items: start;
    gap: clamp(35px, 5vw, 100px);
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 1400px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .st-page .st-heading,
  .st-page .st-copy {
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .st-page .st-number {
    margin-bottom: 25px;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 900;
    line-height: 1.6;
    letter-spacing: 0.09em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .st-page .st-heading h2 {
    font-size: clamp(38px, 4.6vw, 82px);
    font-weight: 900;
    line-height: 0.98;
    letter-spacing: -0.055em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    overflow-wrap: break-word;
  }

  .st-page .st-copy > p {
    margin-bottom: 23px;
    font-size: 18px;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .st-page .st-copy > p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .st-page .st-copy > .st-lead {
    font-size: clamp(21px, 2vw, 27px);
    font-weight: 800;
    line-height: 1.45;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
  }

  /* COLORS */

  .st-page .st-black {
    background: var(--st-black);
    color: var(--st-white);
  }

  .st-page .st-pink {
    background: var(--st-pink);
    color: var(--st-black);
  }

  .st-page .st-yellow {
    background: var(--st-yellow);
    color: var(--st-black);
  }

  .st-page .st-purple {
    background: var(--st-purple);
    color: var(--st-white);
  }

  .st-page .st-black .st-number,
  .st-page .st-purple .st-number {
    color: var(--st-yellow);
  }

  /* LITTLE BOXES */

  .st-page .st-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 16px;
    margin: 30px 0;
  }

  .st-page .st-card {
    min-width: 0;
    padding: 24px;
    border: 2px solid currentColor;
    background: transparent;
    color: inherit;
  }

  .st-page .st-card-label {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 18px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 900;
    line-height: 1.5;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .st-page .st-card h3 {
    margin-bottom: 14px;
    font-size: clamp(21px, 2vw, 29px);
    font-weight: 900;
    line-height: 1.08;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    overflow-wrap: break-word;
  }

  .st-page .st-card p {
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  /* CALLOUTS */

  .st-page .st-callout {
    margin: 30px 0;
    padding: 26px;
    border: 3px solid currentColor;
    font-size: clamp(21px, 2.4vw, 34px);
    font-weight: 900;
    line-height: 1.2;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    overflow-wrap: break-word;
  }

  .st-page .st-black .st-callout,
  .st-page .st-purple .st-callout {
    color: var(--st-yellow);
  }

  .st-page .st-stack {
    display: grid;
    gap: 12px;
    margin: 30px 0;
  }

  .st-page .st-stack p {
    padding: 18px 20px;
    border: 2px solid currentColor;
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 800;
    line-height: 1.5;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  /* PRACTICE BOXES */

  .st-page .st-practice-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 16px;
    margin-top: 28px;
  }

  .st-page .st-practice {
    min-width: 0;
    padding: 24px;
    border: 2px solid currentColor;
  }

  .st-page .st-practice span {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 36px;
    font-weight: 900;
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: -0.05em;
  }

  .st-page .st-practice p {
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  /* ENDING */

  .st-page .st-ending {
    padding: 95px 5vw;
    background: var(--st-black);
    color: var(--st-white);
  }

  .st-page .st-ending-inner {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 1400px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .st-page .st-ending-label {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    color: var(--st-yellow);
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 900;
    line-height: 1.7;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  }

  .st-page .st-ending h2 {
    margin-bottom: 32px;
    font-size: clamp(54px, 8vw, 135px);
    font-weight: 900;
    line-height: 0.93;
    letter-spacing: -0.065em;
  }

  .st-page .st-ending-copy {
    max-width: 620px;
    margin-bottom: 35px;
    font-size: 19px;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .st-page .st-back {
    display: inline-block;
    max-width: 100%;
    padding: 17px 22px;
    border: 2px solid var(--st-yellow);
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--st-yellow);
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 900;
    line-height: 1.5;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition:
      background-color 160ms ease,
      color 160ms ease;
  }

  .st-page .st-back:hover {
    background: var(--st-yellow);
    color: var(--st-black);
  }

  .st-page .st-back:focus-visible {
    outline: 3px solid var(--st-white);
    outline-offset: 5px;
  }

  /* TABLET */

  @media (max-width: 1000px) {
    .st-page .st-inner {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 35px;
      max-width: 850px;
    }

    .st-page .st-heading h2 {
      font-size: clamp(48px, 7vw, 76px);
    }

    .st-page .st-hero-content {
      width: 62%;
    }
  }

  /* MOBILE */

  @media (max-width: 767px) {
    .st-page .st-hero {
      align-items: flex-start;
      min-height: 1000px;
      min-height: max(1000px, 125svh);
      padding: 110px 22px 60px;
    }

    .st-page .st-hero-picture img {
      object-position: center bottom;
    }

    .st-page .st-hero::after {
      background:
        linear-gradient(
          180deg,
          rgba(8, 8, 8, 0.25),
          transparent 70%
        );
    }

    .st-page .st-hero-content {
      width: 100%;
      max-width: 550px;
    }

    .st-page .st-eyebrow {
      margin-bottom: 28px;
      font-size: 10px;
      letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    }

    .st-page .st-hero h1 {
      font-size: clamp(45px, 11.5vw, 85px);
    }

    .st-page .st-intro {
      max-width: 360px;
      margin-top: 27px;
      font-size: 13px;
      line-height: 1.7;
    }

    .st-page .st-section {
      padding: 60px 22px;
    }

    .st-page .st-inner {
      gap: 30px;
    }

    .st-page .st-heading h2 {
      font-size: clamp(39px, 10vw, 66px);
    }

    .st-page .st-number {
      margin-bottom: 20px;
      font-size: 11px;
    }

    .st-page .st-copy > p {
      font-size: 17px;
      line-height: 1.8;
    }

    .st-page .st-grid,
    .st-page .st-practice-grid {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }

    .st-page .st-card h3 {
      font-size: 26px;
    }

    .st-page .st-callout {
      padding: 23px;
      font-size: 25px;
    }

    .st-page .st-ending {
      padding: 70px 22px;
    }

    .st-page .st-ending h2 {
      font-size: clamp(48px, 12vw, 85px);
    }

    .st-page .st-ending-copy {
      font-size: 17px;
    }
  }
</style>


<main class="st-page">

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="st-hero">

    <picture class="st-hero-picture">
      <source
        media="(max-width: 767px)"
        srcset="<%= asset_path('spirituality_shinto_mobile.png') %>"
      >

      <%= image_tag "spirituality_shinto_desktop.png",
          alt: "",
          fetchpriority: "high" %>
    </picture>

    <div class="st-hero-content">

      <p class="st-eyebrow">
        BIPOLAR SOBER / SPIRITUALITY / SHINTO
      </p>

      <h1>
        <span>PAY</span>
        <span>ATTENTION.</span>
        <span>GIVE THANKS.</span>
      </h1>

      <p class="st-intro">
        KAMI. SINCERITY. RENEWAL.<br>
        REVERENCE FOR THE WORLD YOU LIVE IN.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- 01 / INTRODUCTION -->
  <section class="st-section st-black">
    <div class="st-inner">

      <div class="st-heading">
        <p class="st-number">01 / THE WAY OF THE KAMI</p>

        <h2>
          BEGIN WITH<br>
          THE WORLD<br>
          AROUND YOU.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="st-copy">

        <p class="st-lead">
          Through Shinto, you encounter a Japanese tradition
          rooted in reverence, ritual, and relationships.
        </p>

        <p>
          You explore practices shaped by local communities,
          sacred places, mythology, and centuries of observance.
          Shinto is commonly translated as “the Way of the Kami.”
        </p>

        <p>
          As you learn, pay attention to how gratitude,
          sincerity, purification, and community give
          spiritual life a practical expression.
        </p>

        <div class="st-stack">
          <p>What sustains your life?</p>
          <p>What inspires your reverence?</p>
          <p>How do you express gratitude?</p>
          <p>How do you care for your relationships?</p>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 02 / KAMI -->
  <section class="st-section st-pink">
    <div class="st-inner">

      <div class="st-heading">
        <p class="st-number">02 / KAMI</p>

        <h2>
          APPROACH<br>
          WITH<br>
          REVERENCE.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="st-copy">

        <p>
          You encounter kami as divine or sacred beings
          and presences associated with natural phenomena,
          particular places, ancestral figures,
          and extraordinary qualities.
        </p>

        <p>
          Learn about individual kami through their stories,
          shrines, and traditions. The term carries meanings
          that a simple translation such as “god” or “spirit”
          cannot fully express.
        </p>

        <div class="st-grid">

          <div class="st-card">
            <span class="st-card-label">PLACE</span>
            <h3>Land &amp; water.</h3>
            <p>
              You may encounter reverence for kami
              associated with mountains, rivers,
              waterfalls, or particular trees.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="st-card">
            <span class="st-card-label">HISTORY</span>
            <h3>Memory &amp; presence.</h3>
            <p>
              You may learn about kami associated
              with ancestral or historical figures,
              and the communities that honor them.
            </p>
          </div>

        </div>

        <p>
          Let your understanding develop through learning
          about specific traditions and places.
          Avoid assuming that every natural object
          is automatically regarded as a separate kami.
        </p>

      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 03 / NATURE -->
  <section class="st-section st-yellow">
    <div class="st-inner">

      <div class="st-heading">
        <p class="st-number">03 / NATURE &amp; SACRED PLACES</p>

        <h2>
          NOTICE<br>
          WHERE<br>
          YOU ARE.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="st-copy">

        <p>
          You may encounter shrines within wooded grounds
          or closely associated with a particular landscape.
          Sacred trees, rocks, and other places may be
          marked with shimenawa, or sacred ropes.
        </p>

        <p>
          As you approach these places, learn how their
          communities care for them and what respectful
          conduct involves.
        </p>

        <div class="st-grid">

          <div class="st-card">
            <span class="st-card-label">ATTENTION</span>
            <h3>Learn the place.</h3>
            <p>
              Notice its history, landscape, and practices.
              Give your appreciation time to become informed.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="st-card">
            <span class="st-card-label">CARE</span>
            <h3>Respect its boundaries.</h3>
            <p>
              Follow local guidance, protect the environment,
              and leave sacred objects where they belong.
            </p>
          </div>

        </div>

        <div class="st-callout">
          PAY ATTENTION.<br>
          LEARN THE CONTEXT.<br>
          TREAT THE PLACE WITH CARE.
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 04 / HARMONY -->
  <section class="st-section st-purple">
    <div class="st-inner">

      <div class="st-heading">
        <p class="st-number">04 / WA — HARMONY</p>

        <h2>
          CONSIDER<br>
          YOUR PLACE<br>
          IN THE WHOLE.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="st-copy">

        <p>
          Through the value of harmony, you consider
          your relationships with other people,
          your community, nature, and the kami.
        </p>

        <p>
          Your choices influence the conditions you share.
          You can practice cooperation, consideration,
          and responsibility while making room for
          honest disagreement and necessary boundaries.
        </p>

        <div class="st-stack">
          <p>Who will your decision affect?</p>
          <p>What commitment needs your attention?</p>
          <p>Where could you offer practical care?</p>
          <p>What relationship needs repair?</p>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 05 / PURIFICATION -->
  <section class="st-section st-black">
    <div class="st-inner">

      <div class="st-heading">
        <p class="st-number">05 / PURIFICATION &amp; RENEWAL</p>

        <h2>
          MAKE ROOM<br>
          TO BEGIN<br>
          AGAIN.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="st-copy">

        <p>
          In Shinto, you encounter practices of purification
          that prepare you to approach sacred spaces
          and renew relationships with the kami.
        </p>

        <p>
          You may also encounter the term kegare:
          ritual impurity associated in some contexts
          with death, blood, illness, or disruption.
          This ritual category should not become a judgment
          of your worth or anyone else's.
        </p>

        <div class="st-grid">

          <div class="st-card">
            <span class="st-card-label">HARAE</span>
            <h3>Purification rites.</h3>
            <p>
              You may participate in rites involving
              prayers and ritual actions, often
              conducted by Shinto priests.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="st-card">
            <span class="st-card-label">MISOGI</span>
            <h3>Water purification.</h3>
            <p>
              You encounter traditions of purification
              through water, practiced within
              particular settings and guidance.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="st-card">
            <span class="st-card-label">TEMIZU</span>
            <h3>Before approaching.</h3>
            <p>
              At many shrines, you cleanse your hands
              and mouth according to local guidance
              before worship.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="st-card">
            <span class="st-card-label">RENEWAL</span>
            <h3>Return with care.</h3>
            <p>
              You can reflect on preparation, renewal,
              and approaching your relationships
              with fresh attention.
            </p>
          </div>

        </div>

        <p>
          Ritual renewal can accompany practical repair.
          You still attend to harm, responsibilities,
          and the care a situation requires.
        </p>

      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 06 / SINCERITY -->
  <section class="st-section st-pink">
    <div class="st-inner">

      <div class="st-heading">
        <p class="st-number">06 / MAKOTO — SINCERITY</p>

        <h2>
          BRING<br>
          YOUR WHOLE<br>
          FUCKING HEART.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="st-copy">

        <p class="st-lead">
          Through makoto, you cultivate sincerity,
          honesty, and integrity in your conduct.
        </p>

        <p>
          Bring genuine attention to your prayers,
          offerings, and relationships. Let your intentions
          become visible through the way you act.
        </p>

        <p>
          You express sincerity when you keep a commitment,
          admit what happened, offer gratitude,
          or acknowledge what you do not understand.
        </p>

        <div class="st-callout">
          WHAT DOES YOUR INTENTION<br>
          LOOK LIKE IN YOUR ACTIONS?
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 07 / GRATITUDE -->
  <section class="st-section st-yellow">
    <div class="st-inner">

      <div class="st-heading">
        <p class="st-number">07 / GRATITUDE &amp; OFFERINGS</p>

        <h2>
          RECOGNIZE<br>
          WHAT<br>
          SUSTAINS YOU.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="st-copy">

        <p>
          Your life depends on food, water, sunlight,
          the land, and the contributions of others.
          Gratitude gives you a way to acknowledge
          those relationships.
        </p>

        <p>
          At shrines, you may encounter offerings such as
          rice, water, salt, and sake. Their meaning belongs
          to the ritual and community in which they are offered.
        </p>

        <div class="st-grid">

          <div class="st-card">
            <span class="st-card-label">REVERENCE</span>
            <h3>Offer thanks.</h3>
            <p>
              Recognize what you receive and approach
              your offering with respect and sincerity.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="st-card">
            <span class="st-card-label">RELATIONSHIP</span>
            <h3>Keep showing up.</h3>
            <p>
              Cultivate an ongoing practice of attention
              rather than treating an offering
              as a guaranteed exchange for a favor.
            </p>
          </div>

        </div>

        <p>
          In your own practice, choose forms of gratitude
          compatible with your sobriety. You can learn
          about appropriate water or rice offerings
          without keeping alcohol in your home.
        </p>

      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 08 / COMMUNITY AND SEASONS -->
  <section class="st-section st-purple">
    <div class="st-inner">

      <div class="st-heading">
        <p class="st-number">08 / COMMUNITY, MEMORY &amp; SEASONS</p>

        <h2>
          PARTICIPATE<br>
          IN A<br>
          SHARED WORLD.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="st-copy">

        <p>
          Through festivals, ceremonies, and seasonal
          observances, you encounter spiritual life
          practiced within a community.
        </p>

        <p>
          You may see gratitude for harvests, celebrations
          of new beginnings, and rituals marking
          important transitions.
        </p>

        <div class="st-grid">

          <div class="st-card">
            <span class="st-card-label">MATSURI</span>
            <h3>Gather &amp; celebrate.</h3>
            <p>
              You encounter festivals honoring kami
              and sustaining relationships between
              shrines and their communities.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="st-card">
            <span class="st-card-label">SEASONAL OBSERVANCE</span>
            <h3>Mark the change.</h3>
            <p>
              You acknowledge the passage of time
              and the conditions that support
              growth and renewal.
            </p>
          </div>

        </div>

        <p>
          You can also learn how family and ancestral
          observances connect generations. Keep their
          cultural context in view: Japanese ancestral
          practices often draw on Buddhist and other
          traditions alongside Shinto.
        </p>

      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 09 / CONDUCT -->
  <section class="st-section st-black">
    <div class="st-inner">

      <div class="st-heading">
        <p class="st-number">09 / CONDUCT &amp; RESTORATION</p>

        <h2>
          CARE FOR<br>
          WHAT YOU<br>
          ARE PART OF.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="st-copy">

        <p>
          You can explore ethical conduct through sincerity,
          respect, and your responsibility to the relationships
          that sustain your life.
        </p>

        <p>
          When you cause harm, consider what acknowledgment,
          correction, and repair require.
          Give your spiritual intentions a practical expression.
        </p>

        <div class="st-stack">
          <p>Tell the truth about what happened.</p>
          <p>Listen to the people affected.</p>
          <p>Address what you can repair.</p>
          <p>Follow through on realistic commitments.</p>
        </div>

        <p>
          You can take wrongdoing seriously while remaining
          open to change. What you do next matters
          to the relationships you want to maintain.
        </p>

      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


